<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.240
<b><i>#ENCODERGASM PRESENTS</i></b>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:20.240
<i>toki ga mirai ni susumu to dare ga kimeta no da?</i>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:20.240
<b>Who decided that time should move forward towards the future?</b>

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:26.830
<i>rakuin o kesu inochi ga rekishi o kakinaosu</i>

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:26.830
<b>The lives that will erase these brands will rewrite history</b>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:34.840
<i>utsukushii tsurugi wa hito to hito tsunagete</i>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:34.840
<b>People are connected by beautiful, double-edged swords</b>

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:44.770
<i>meguri kuru setsuna sa kanashimi wo aratte</i>

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>Our coming anticipation will wash away our sadness</b>

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:53.780
<i>anata to no aida ni inochi aru katachi wo</i>

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:53.780
<b>With you, between us, life is formed</b>

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:05.120
<i>Kono hoshi ni sasageru ai to iu shirushi de</i>

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:05.120
<b>With the proof called "love" that we offer to this planet</b>

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:06.080
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:06.580
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:07.580
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.080
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:08.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.210
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.590
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.090
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:14.590
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.590
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:29.260
<i>I was shocked to discover that Queen Dianna and Milady Kihel had switched places without any of us knowing,</i>

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:30.810
<i>But afterwards...</i>

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:33.290
<i>They each managed to perform one another's tasks perfectly.</i>

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:36.200
<i>It made me admire them both.</i>

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:41.950
<i>Especially Kihel, when she had to substitute for Queen Dianna...</i>

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:46.280
<i>...in giving the speech to overrule the previous decision to found a fiefdom. l was speechless.</i>

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.760
<b>Sochie's War</b>

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:02.460
Hey hey, I told you to put your best foot forward!

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:06.880
If you're up top, dig by hand! I told you not to use the machines, didn't I?

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:13.100
- Can't the Kapool bring it here for us?
- Your hands would be more suitable for the job.

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:18.280
What's this about!?

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.990
After all that hard work digging out that huge hunk of metal... they just treat us like garbage!

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.080
No kidding!

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:28.330
That's just it. The people supervising this now are all Moonrace members. What a joke.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:32.170
Who was it who worked to excavate this flying machine?

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.880
It was all of you.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:37.170
So this ship should belong to us soldiers of the Militia!

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.090
I don't care if you have professional technicians or not...

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:42.390
...how can you let our enemy sit here with us and tweak these systems like they own them?

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:46.470
Do you people have the technical capacity to make this "Willgem" work?

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:50.980
This should be the control route for the SR Laser...

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.560
It's rather sophisticated.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:53.980
Those jerks...

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.440
I don't think we could do it ourselves.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.070
You are such a loser!

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.990
I can't do anything about it...

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:04.360
It's a fact we just can't deny. The truth is what it is.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.960
It was quite a find. Still, even I don't know how to operate it.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.380
It lacks either wheels or caterpillar treads.

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:23.260
It uses a hover system to move.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:26.350
A hover system?

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:30.390
It glides over the ground on a cushion created by air pressure.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:33.060
There's a jet engine in it, right?

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.390
Yes. We found the vent for one.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:40.890
- Ladderum... is it really that large?
- Yes.

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:47.780
Pull!

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.090
Do you know what this is, Chief Engineer Horace?

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:00.090
Yes. It's called Nano-skin, and it dissolves upon contact with the air.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:04.970
This is what protected the buried Mechanical Dolls?

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.970
Additionally, it assimilates itself into the ground to help cover the relics.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:10.180
I can't say I understand it well...

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:13.190
I'll take some time to guide you through the basics of nano-technology later...

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:17.190
But the Mustached Mobile Suit got banged in the head pretty badly, didn't it?

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.480
Hmm? Oh, it's rather odd.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.780
The damage doesn't seem ordinary.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:26.990
Recently, the surface of the head started to be enveloped by some sort of odd rust.

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:29.160
Then we'll remove the head and examine it.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.000
Remove the head?

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.580
Loran, this window's still open.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.460
Please don't touch anything, Milady Kihel.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:37.880
Your hands will become dirty.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:39.670
The resemblance is uncanny...

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.880
Loran, this vehicle now belongs to you.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.050
Why choose me?

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:46.760
You are now its Captain. I expect you to make good use of it.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.600
Meaning that it's up to me to get it operational...

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.100
You'll be able to do that easily, Loran.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.060
Well, that's...

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:53.390
l'll assist you.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:56.100
Please don't joke like that, Your Majesty Dianna.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.400
My name is Kihel.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:03.270
Sir Guin, I'm here to help out too!

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:06.110
Amazing! It's incredible!

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:08.280
This machine even gives us a means to service Mobile Suits!

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:10.480
Not to mention a place to rest.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:15.000
What do you think you're doing?

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.460
I never heard of this washing basin thing.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:20.590
Sid found it inside there.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:24.800
l never expected that doing Laundry like this would be so enjoyable!

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:27.510
Please don't do that for me, it isn't proper!

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:29.470
- What do you mean?
-That's not...

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:30.890
Earth women do this, right?

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:32.880
Those are my underpants!

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:37.560
It's so cold...

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:38.900
- Loran...
- Yes?

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:42.480
This machine can be used for more than a simple repair station.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:44.990
It can move much faster than a swift gallop, can't it?

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:46.280
Gallop?

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:49.490
Sir Guin wishes to progress quickly enough to outrun a horse, doesn't he?

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.780
Do you think I can?

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:53.790
You are a Militia Pilot. Of course you can.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.910
- Or am I wrong?
- Well, not quite...

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:59.080
You're still part of Dianna Counter...are you sure about this?

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.960
A power such as this does not put my people in any danger.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:07.090
Under the command of a great Captain who dislikes war, I have nothing to fear.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:09.390
Thank you.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:14.970
When Miss Kihel stopped being Kihel, she began shining brighter than ever.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:17.120
That's right.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:22.480
We are from the same planet. We should be able to find a way to make this a land of peace.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:26.490
Kihel said exactly what I'm feeling. Her speech rejected plans to forcibly establish a nation.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:30.690
When I heard her, I started shivering with excitement.

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:33.200
Kihel shouldn't be the only one.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:37.000
l too have things that I must do as well.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.000
Umm...

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.290
What is it?

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:42.290
Are you really Queen Dianna?

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.340
You keep asking me these strange questions.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:48.050
But you act and speak exactly the same as Lady Kihel.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:50.260
It's natural for you to see it that way.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:51.970
This is Queen Dianna?

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:53.180
Ahh, there you are.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:54.100
Yes?

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.270
C'mon, Horace is about to give his demonstration.

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:57.270
Chief Horace?

00:06:57.470 --> 00:06:58.680
At your service.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:00.060
l am Loran Cehack.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:02.980
I never expected that the pilot of the White Doll would be so young!

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:06.480
Isn't the Mustached mechanical doll's armor rather amazing?

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:08.280
That's right, it is.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:10.990
A nanomachine is even smaller than a human body cell.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:15.910
They can be used to reconstruct any part of the body down to the smallest part.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:19.080
If you look at it closely, you'll notice the Mustached shape's been fully restored.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:22.120
The original design's been recreated beneath this gritty substance.

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:24.080
Look!

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.300
It can fix the warped mustache?

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.590
That's exactly right.

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:28.960
Nanomachinery technology....

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.380
Is something you have you understand in order to build cities on the moon.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:35.170
But I've never seen anything so advanced that it can heal itself like an actual life form.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:42.480
It's already finished...

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.150
Then, will it look like this beneath the substance?

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:48.980
Not exactly. No metal alloy alone can do what this substance does.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.070
Then...

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:52.700
Are you using the nanites to repair other sections internally, Mr. Ladderum?

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.620
That's correct. I never would have known any of this without Horace' contributions.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.990
I am curious, though.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:03.080
This could very well be the mobile suit "Gundam" from the old legends.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:05.540
What's a "Gundam"?

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:07.590
According to the Moonrace's legends...

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:12.170
The Gundam was the most violent nemesis of the space immigrants.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:15.470
But...Before we found ourselves underneath Mountain Cycle...

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:18.880
No one here had ever even mentioned the name Gundam before.

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:21.090
Well, anyhow...

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:23.270
That hurt, you know...

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:27.610
I'm here so I can have Horace teach me about the technology we unearthed from the Mountain cycles.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:32.570
No no! I'M the one who's here to learn about the technologies needed to live on Earth.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:33.990
Well put.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:36.490
It's got me rarin' to go as well!

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:38.490
I want to study the relics left by our ancestors,

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:42.510
in order to understand what happened to earth in the past.

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:45.290
So what in the world will we name this vehicle?

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:46.920
Is it called a "Heavy Box"?

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.130
Why not call it "Gallop"?

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.800
Gallop?

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:53.300
Can this vehicle move that quickly without wheels?

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.590
Horace did give us his guarantee that it would.

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:58.760
Gallop Captain! I look forward to working with you from now on!

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:02.880
- Lord Guin has made this decision.
- That may be so, but...

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:09.150
You were looking for me?

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.070
- Please, explain it to me.
- Ma'am?

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:15.860
My announcement will cause many problems among our people. I already realize that.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:19.320
The issues lie with a specific faction of our army who seeks to expand the war.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.370
Yes, but I'd like to get to the essence of the problem.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:22.790
Yes?

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:25.660
Some among us wish to undermine the authority of Dianna as Queen...

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:29.040
Who are these people?

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:32.380
It's probably those of the moderate faction who remain loyal to Agrippa.

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:34.670
Then what's their true reasoning?

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:36.960
Their real reasons?

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:40.680
In order to return to the Earth...

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:44.680
...the Moonrace has been forced to wait patiently for over a thousand years.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:48.770
But when the moment finally came, some among them began to have a change of heart.

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:50.560
A change of heart?

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.480
Time has been known to change people.

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:53.980
However...

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:55.780
...for as long as l am here with you...

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:59.530
I will defend you with my life, Your Majesty!

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:02.660
Harry, I appreciate your feelings...

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:05.500
But are you sure that you really mean that?

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:08.960
Well, are you losing your trust in me, Queen Dianna?

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:10.580
That's not...

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:13.670
I'm very happy to hear you say that, Lieutenant Harry.

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:17.130
Then can we just continue on as we always have?

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:19.380
Of course we can.

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:25.560
To think we'd let the Militia barbarians surround the Soleil...

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:27.140
We have to gun them down first!

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:31.310
We need to make it clear that the land we're on is now our own, correct?

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:35.190
Some professional technicians have defected to the Militia.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:39.780
Not realizing that the Earth had Mobile suits was the biggest mistake we ever could have made...

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:41.280
Don't cry about it!

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:42.980
I'm not crying!

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:47.790
Let's do something about it, Commander!

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:50.000
What are you talking about?

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:53.880
We'll wipe out everything the technicians want to study!

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:56.090
That's right! A preemptive attack!

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.510
This isn't even a war!

00:10:57.670 --> 00:10:59.970
We haven't yet received orders saying we can't blow them to pieces

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:01.170
Right.

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:05.260
I'll give you a ride.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:07.560
You need to stay and make the Gallop operational.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:11.190
Wait a moment, the engine seems to be having troubles.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:12.980
Well...

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:19.150
The one who tried to assassinate Lady Kihel, Ms. Teteth... I'm still worried about that situation.

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:20.450
And?

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:25.280
I would like to use the Gallop to find and ask her why she did it.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:28.750
But I'm not sure if I should use the Gallop for such things.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.500
You're the Captain, aren't you?

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:33.170
Shouldn't you be the one who makes that decision?

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:36.130
You mean I'm allowed to do that?

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:50.980
Loran, there's something I had to come here and tell you!

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:52.890
Milady Sochie?

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:53.970
Sochie?

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:07.080
Cleanup on the deck is complete.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:09.290
All we need to do is remove the Nanoskin on the underbelly.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:10.500
Roger!

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:12.790
Why didn't you reject it?

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:14.370
Why would you accept?

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:18.300
With the threat of war, everyone has to see to their own responsibilities.

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:20.800
So, that should apply to me as well.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.670
This isn't good for the Militia.

00:12:25.610 --> 00:12:30.100
Ameria needs you to fight for her on the front lines, yet you don't care about that at all.

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:35.190
Letting someone like you get this wonderful machine which can help mobilize and maintain our own mechanical dolls...

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.560
It's like casting pearls before swine!

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:40.360
If they request my assistance in their plan, I'd still go and fight!

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.990
We're out there fighting every day!

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:45.860
But out here, you wouldn't hear even a single cannon shot!

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:48.950
You're just stuck here with my sister, wasting time and space!

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:51.500
Frankly, you're just trying to chase my sister's tail...

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.000
Lady, it's time to go...

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.080
Please hold on for just a second!

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:58.960
Sister, don't you think that this vehicle would better suit Miashei and myself?

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:01.300
Ask Sir Guin to reconsider, please!

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.300
l have no worries about any of that.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:06.220
Loran will complete anything that he needs to.

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:09.970
Sister... Do you really think so?

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:12.970
Honestly, while Loran's chasing my tail...

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:16.310
I can still oversee how he handles the White Doll.

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:19.180
Loran, I leave the Gallop to you.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:21.270
Sister, wait!

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:39.960
From this moment forward, this machine will serve as my mechanical doll, the Kapool's, base of operations!

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:41.870
What the?

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:45.550
You'll ruin this place if you force it in like that!

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:50.100
This is now my territory!

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.600
Will this serve as a front line base for mechanical dolls?

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:54.890
It was worth excavating.

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:58.060
I wish I could work on it like those mechanics!

00:13:58.060 --> 00:13:59.980
Gotta go where we're told.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:02.180
It'd save us a lot of walking, right?

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:24.460
A vehicle this large is just begging for our enemies to attack it. I'm not sure if I like it.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:25.800
Ahh, there it is.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:26.670
What?

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:28.090
It's this thing's manual.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:31.090
l had this computer make a "print out".

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:32.470
Mr. Ladderum?

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:36.770
To the left of the wheel, there's a switch for adjusting the skirt's angle. Flip it to neutral.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:39.180
This one?

00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:47.360
It doesn't explain how we set up this tent...

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:48.570
I guess not.

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:51.780
Well then, I'll go figure out how we'll put the mustache's head back on.

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.070
Sorry about all this.

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:54.490
Where are we heading?

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:55.660
We're patrolling.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:57.870
Can't you let me do my job like the Lady told me too?

00:14:57.870 --> 00:14:59.870
I see. Have you seen any sign of the enemy?

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:02.790
I'm waiting to see if we're able to draw out the enemy's attention like bait.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.960
Bait? Like bait, you say?

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:07.500
Well, you can count on me if any enemy should show up!

00:15:08.230 --> 00:15:11.840
They taught me how to use vulcans, and I brought extra missiles along for the trip.

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:16.100
Heck, just yesterday I took down a mechanical doll by myself.

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:17.810
You defeated a mobile suit?

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:22.890
Right, so you won't always be able to treat me like my sister's follower.

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:25.980
I never thought of you like that...

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:39.080
Lieutenant Poe, we've detected an unknown object, but I can't see it.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:40.290
Can you?

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.830
There, 18 Degrees to the right! An object that's not in our database.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:44.880
I'm analyzing it.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:47.050
I can't get a clear look at it because of the distortion from earth's heat...

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:49.380
Freeze frame and enhance.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:51.170
Could that be...

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:54.430
That's the Mustached mobile suit...

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.970
Are they transporting it for repairs?

00:15:58.530 --> 00:16:01.180
It's the Mustached Mobile Suit, or perhaps should I say, the "Gundam".

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:02.850
Our objective's now to capture it!

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:06.360
Aren't we here to investigate the Spaceship's Mountain Cycle?

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:08.860
We're capturing the Mustache! Is that understood?

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:11.070
Roger that, Lieutenant.

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:13.070
Do you see it?

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:14.990
The giant scarecrows are coming!

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:16.370
Are you sure about that?

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:17.780
I see three of them!

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:20.370
Mr. Ladderum, let's get moving!

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:21.580
Why!?

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:23.670
The White Doll's still being repaired!

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:26.000
I say that we should stay here and fight them!

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.660
Milady!

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:30.170
Don't be so rude!

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:31.380
l am going off to fight!

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:32.790
Milady!

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:34.970
- Mr. Ladderum!
 - What's wrong?

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:37.430
Get the White Doll's head reattached, please! I'm heading out!

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:41.980
I don't understand how we launch it... and how do I operate this Radar thing?

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:43.270
What?

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:44.560
Three "Scarecrows"...

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:46.260
Any more? No...

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:50.570
Lady Sochie is heading out?

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:52.690
Hurry up and get us out of here, please.

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:54.700
Milady Sochie, don't go!

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:56.110
Those scarecrow's cannons pack a punch, don't they?

00:16:56.360 --> 00:17:00.120
If we get hit, the Gallop wouldn't stand a chance!

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:03.000
Mr. Horace, Could you please get the White Doll's head reattached?

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.000
What's going on?

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.500
A team of WaDoms has found us!

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:06.790
Oh, this isn't good...

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.500
I can stop them with the White Doll.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:12.460
Then, is that girl going off to fight against a team of WaDoms?

00:17:14.440 --> 00:17:16.970
Dianna Counter, Here I...

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:19.090
No, don't change directions now!

00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:23.760
Ladderum, we can't run away, we have to fight!

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:28.650
Milady, please stay where you are!

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:38.410
- Escape on that road to the right.
- Roger.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:39.990
Are the cannons operational?

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.690
I'll talk to Chief Horace.

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:45.790
Loran, can you hear me?

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:47.960
Once you've snapped the head in place, it'll reconnect all hardware itself.

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:49.170
Roger that!

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:50.990
Where's Lady Sochie now...?

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:01.300
Papa, please protect me.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:03.590
The scarecrows are only aiming at the Gallop?

00:18:05.530 --> 00:18:07.060
That's rude.

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:10.690
l shouldn't always need to take orders from my servant.

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:16.030
Alright, the target!

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:18.900
Did you lose your head, Mustache?

00:18:23.930 --> 00:18:26.000
I'll be your opponent now!

00:18:28.930 --> 00:18:30.290
What the...!?

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:32.540
Chase down the mobile suit on our tail!

00:18:32.810 --> 00:18:34.790
The White Doll is mine!

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:41.170
- Have any of our men manned the turrets yet?
- Yes, they have.

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:08.070
I apologize!

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:14.580
My father will keep me safe!

00:19:17.650 --> 00:19:19.380
One of them can't use their legs...

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:21.170
Where's Lady Sochie?

00:19:22.110 --> 00:19:24.530
Hey Loran, your shield and rifle are ready!

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:26.310
The cannons are ready now, Ladderum!

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:28.270
You got that, right-side turret?

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:29.480
What about the left turret?

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:33.590
You read me, Horace? Ahh, There's no time for a test shot, just shoot them!

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:35.270
I'm going full speed!

00:19:40.420 --> 00:19:42.990
Are you kidding? No way, you won't capture me!

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:48.660
Go ahead and kill me!

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:51.830
I'll just meet my father in heaven. I'm not scared at all!

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:58.340
You can't always be lucky, Mustache!

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:03.170
Fire!

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:12.180
What good will clipping my nails do!?

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:18.980
Milady is...!

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:33.580
Where's the Gallop?

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:36.210
Milady, are you alright? Milady!

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:38.960
Please answer me, are you okay?

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:41.210
Please give me some sort of answer!

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:43.470
I was rescued by my own servant again...

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:54.980
Two people were killed?

00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:56.480
Where at?

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:59.270
It happened because I gave a reckless order.

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:02.360
Unfortunately, that's the risk of using an unknown ancient vehicle.

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:04.980
No one can take direct responsibility for it.

00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:24.380
A drink?

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:26.790
Forgive me, Milady.

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:34.680
It's really my fault that those people had to die.

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:36.970
I only made things worse for you, Loran...

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:43.390
They say it's easy for a person to accept piloting a mechanical doll because you can't see the people you're fighting against.

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:52.070
Yet today, I can't help but to wonder who the pilots of the enemy Mobile Suits are.

00:21:53.140 --> 00:21:55.040
And even so, you still continue fighting.

00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:57.780
You really are amazing, Loran.

00:21:58.430 --> 00:22:02.620
It's not me. It's that thing... the White Doll, that's so amazing.

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:40.330 --> 00:23:42.770
<i>In war, one rarely gets to choose their own battlefield.</i>

00:23:42.770 --> 00:23:46.070
<i>Yet even when Dianna Counter invades her territory...</i>

00:23:46.070 --> 00:23:48.160
<i>The old woman, Anis, refuses to evacuate her farmland.</i>

00:23:49.450 --> 00:23:51.990
<i>Even that Donkey of hers was telling us to leave...</i>

00:23:51.990 --> 00:23:56.680
<i>So I tried to forcibly evacuate her to safety, but we ended up reading a mysterious letter instead.</i>

00:23:58.070 --> 00:24:00.280
<i>Next Time... on </i>TURN A GUNDAM...

00:24:00.730 --> 00:24:02.320
Anis' Power

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:05.240
"Some people will even fight the wind itself!"

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:08.420
<b>Anis' Power</b>
